#
# hvdcp_opti (vendor_hvdcp): 5.15 charging uses IIO channels. It scans
#   /sys/bus/iio/devices/*/name (96 + 92 denials on img146: "devices" dir and
#   "name" files, label sysfs). The IIO devices are under the SPMI PMICs:
#     .../spmi-0/0-00/...pm8150@0:vadc@3100/iio:device0
#     .../spmi-0/0-02/...pm8150b@2:vadc@3100/iio:device1
#     .../spmi-0/0-02/...pm8150b@2:qcom,qpnp-smb5/iio:device3
#     .../spmi-0/0-02/...pm8150b@2:qpnp,fg/iio:device4
#     .../spmi-0/0-04/...pm8150l@4:vadc@3100/iio:device2
#   The 4.19 policy only gives it sysfs_charger (smb1390 nodes, not on timelm).
#   Needs a type for these iio devices plus an allow rule for vendor_hvdcp,
#   not just a label. Revisit with the hvdcp_opti crash loop (backlog item 4).
#
# Not present on 5.15 / this kernel, vendor rule just stops matching (no action
# unless a user of the node shows up in denials):
#   ae00000.qcom.qcom,mdss_mdp/caps          (typo path in vendor; no caps node on 5.15 SDE)
#   ae00000.../mdss_fb_primary/leds, /devices/virtual/graphics/fb0|fb1/*   (no fbdev on 5.15 DRM)
#   soc:qcom,dsi-display-primary/{acl,cabc,dc,hbm}  (LiveDisplay uses /devices/virtual/panel/img_tune, already labelled by hardware/lge)
#   soc:qcom,smp2p-{adsp,cdsp,dsps,modem}/wakeup (5.15 smp2p has no per-edge wakeup source; only soc:qcom,smp2p_sleepstate/wakeup)
#   bolero va/wsa swr_ctrl wakeup               (no wakeup source on 5.15 swr master)
#   coresight stm/tmc-etr/tmc-etf/swao-csr, soc:hwevent  (QDSS/coresight drivers not built)
#   5c00000.qcom,ssc/subsys2, subsys7/state     (4.19 subsystem_restart; 5.15 is remoteproc-slpi.
#                                                 Our msm_subsys compat only exposes esoc0. Check the sensors HAL denials once enforcing.)
#   soc:fingerprint@0/wakeup/wakeup7            (vendor hardcodes the number; 5.15 has wakeup40. Covered if the
#                                                 fingerprint wakeup needs a label: genfscon sysfs /devices/platform/soc/soc:fingerprint@0/wakeup)
#   990000.i2c/i2c-1/1-0061 wireless            (IDT P9222 wireless charger, not in our DT)
#   vendor:lge-veneer-psy, vendor:lge_usb_ds2/ds3, lge-unified-nodes, battery_current_limit (LG drivers not ported)
#   /devices/virtual/panel/panel-0/brightness  (ours is /devices/virtual/panel/brightness, already labelled)
#
# Other img146 denials, not labels:
#   vendor_qti_init_shell setattr sysfs "uevent" (3), vendor_init write debugfs "debug_suspend",
#   vendor_init create "ipa", system_server setsched on ksu (KSU domain), kernel read of
#   libQSEEComAPI.so / keymaster (our uldump debug, goes with the §11 strip).
#
# Regenerate: kernel workspace tmp/rom-sepolicy/{resolve,gen}.py against a fresh live listing
#   (adb shell find /sys/devices -xdev > live-sysfs-all.txt) after the kernel cleanup,
#   since device names can still change then.
